30,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The island houses are cheap per person, but all-in rates mean light eaters pay as much as big eaters.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The ferry takes two whole days, but the train to the valley is only ninety minutes.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Separate rooms caused a huge price difference last time. A single bill for a whole building is much fairer.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The inn has strict mealtimes and we'd all be on futons in one room. That sounds exhausting.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Last year we were too separate. But in a shared house, there's absolutely no place to be alone.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, if the island house is one bill, does that solve the pricing problem?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Takumi, if you hate the inn's rules, the city has no timetables.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, yes, a single building bill divides evenly, which is the most logical way to avoid disputes.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, that's true. I can't stand the idea of a shared room with everyone on futons.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"We need a balance. The city might be too disconnected, but a single house is too crowded.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Rin,,I just want to know the total cost upfront. The island seems cheapest for the stay itself.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,The island is a travel nightmare. Two days gone? No thanks. The valley or city is better.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The city beds are expensive and vary wildly. The island or the valley is more predictable.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Takumi,,The island houses only have one bathroom and the water gets cold. I can't do that.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we go to the city, we risk repeating last year's mistake of not actually spending time together.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Rin,,So the island is cheap but the bathroom is bad and the travel is long?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. The valley is fast to reach, though the buses there are limited.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Asuka,,The valley inn is a fixed rate. It's clean and the cost is transparent.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Takumi,,But the valley inn has those strict mealtimes and shared rooms. I'd prefer the city.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Toshio,,The valley inn forces us to be together without the claustrophobia of a single rented house.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
